[17592186537865 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "df5421c1-33c8-52c3-a934-b3f293d407a7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537866 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186537532 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537866 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537866 #edb/ref 1077 "field-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537866 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186537532 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537866 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e0ee657f-8a91-5462-a83e-e961791c1d5e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537867 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186537448 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537867 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537867 #edb/ref 1077 "field-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537867 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186537448 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537867 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e84af63e-7ff1-5d27-8af7-764ee61799ab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537885 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186537790 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537885 #edb/ref 1069 "q-97017" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537885 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537885 #edb/ref 1071 "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2{cosh}^{2}⁡2x+2{sinh}^{2}⁡2x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537885 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1212fe46-96e8-51be-81fa-22f7749ff713" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537885 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the following double-angle formula for cosine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the following double-angle formula for the hyperbolic cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2\\theta ={cosh}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sinh}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =2x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cosh}⁡4x={cosh}^{2}⁡2x+{sinh}^{2}⁡2x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2{cosh}^{2}⁡2x+2{sinh}^{2}⁡4x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }({cosh}^{2}⁡2x+{sinh}^{2}⁡4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cosh}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡4x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡4\\pi -\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡4\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537886 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186537764 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537886 #edb/ref 1069 "q-97085" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537886 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537886 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate ${\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(1-16{sinh}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537886 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "12bc09cc-29a3-5e9b-995b-e577844956a7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537886 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the following double-angle formula for cosine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the following double-angle formula for the hyperbolic cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x=1+2{sinh}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n{sinh}^{2}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x-1).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(1-16{sinh}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}[1-16\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x-1)]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(9-8\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(9x-4\\operatorname{sinh}⁡2x)\\,{|}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\  & =[9\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-4\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)]-[9\\cdot 0-4\\operatorname{sinh}⁡0] \\\\  & =9\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-4\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-{e}^{-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}}{2} \\\\  & =9\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-2({2}^{2}-{2}^{-2}) \\\\  & =9\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\frac{15}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537887 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186537772 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537887 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186537844 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537887 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186537863 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537887 #edb/ref 1069 "q-351902" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537887 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537887 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the following integral.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}({cosh}^{2}⁡x+3)\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}}\n$\\operatorname{sinh}⁡($\n {{field-2}}\n$)\\,+\\,$\n {{field-3}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537887 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "12efb8aa-cbcc-5328-91fe-5d769b12ac7b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537887 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the following double-angle formula for cosine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -1\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the following double-angle formula for the hyperbolic cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2\\theta =2{cosh}^{2}⁡\\theta -1\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cosh}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2\\theta +1).\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =x$, we have\n\n$$\n{cosh}^{2}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}({cosh}^{2}⁡x+3)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x+1)+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x+\\frac{7}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡2x+\\frac{7}{2}x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\frac{7}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}]-[\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡0+0] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(\\pi )+\\frac{7\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537891 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186537840 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537891 #edb/ref 1069 "q-97073" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537891 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537891 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\int (4{sinh}^{2}⁡2x+3)\\,\\text{d}x=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537891 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1ddb9340-9af2-51a6-8581-bb4c21f42fab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537891 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the following double-angle formula for cosine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the following double-angle formula for the hyperbolic cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2\\theta =1+2{sinh}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n{sinh}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2\\theta -1).\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =2x$, we have\n\n$$\n{sinh}^{2}⁡2x=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡4x-1).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (4{sinh}^{2}⁡2x+3)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡4x-1)+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡4x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡4x+x+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡4x+x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537892 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186537806 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537892 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186537850 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537892 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186537865 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537892 #edb/ref 1069 "q-351898" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537892 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537892 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the following integral.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}({cosh}^{2}⁡(\\frac{3x}{2})+1)\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}}\n$\\operatorname{sinh}⁡($\n{{field-2}}\n$)+\\,$\n{{field-3}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537892 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1ebb4c16-c258-518a-a825-ce276a761a9f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537892 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the following double-angle formula for cosine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -1\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the following double-angle formula for the hyperbolic cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2\\theta =2{cosh}^{2}⁡\\theta -1\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cosh}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2\\theta +1).\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{3x}{2}$, we have\n\n$$\n{cosh}^{2}⁡(\\frac{3x}{2})=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡3x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}({cosh}^{2}⁡(\\frac{3x}{2})+1)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡3x+1)+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡3x+\\frac{3}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡3x+\\frac{3}{2}x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})+\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4}]-[\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡0+0] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\,\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})+\\frac{3\\pi }{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537895 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186537841 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537895 #edb/ref 1069 "q-97010" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537895 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537895 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\int (\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x(2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x+1)+\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x(2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x-1))\\,\\text{d}x=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537895 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "216e3ef8-6751-5e3e-9d7f-5d48b7476c3e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537895 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the following double-angle formula for cosine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x={cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the following double-angle formula for the hyperbolic cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x={cosh}^{2}⁡x+{sinh}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\int (\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x(2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x+1)+\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x(2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x-1))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & \\,=\\int (2{cosh}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x+2{sinh}^{2}⁡x-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & \\,=\\int (2({cosh}^{2}⁡x+{sinh}^{2}⁡x)+\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & \\,=\\int (2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x+\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & \\,=2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡2x+\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x-\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x+C \\\\  & \\,=\\operatorname{sinh}⁡2x+\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x-\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537898 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186537781 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537898 #edb/ref 1069 "q-97002" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537898 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537898 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\int 4\\operatorname{sinh}⁡3x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537898 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2aefbec7-dbc4-5c5a-8816-9b24bf877b40" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537898 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the double-angle formula for the hyperbolic sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sinh}⁡2\\theta =2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cosh}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\n \n\nLetting $\\theta =3x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡6x=2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡3x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡3x\\,⇒\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡6x=\\operatorname{sinh}⁡3x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡3x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 4\\operatorname{sinh}⁡3x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x & =4\\int \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{sinh}⁡6x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int \\operatorname{sinh}⁡6x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{6}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡6x+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡6x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537909 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186537825 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537909 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186537842 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537909 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186537866 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537909 #edb/ref 1069 "q-352792" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537909 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537909 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}(8{sinh}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})-4)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\operatorname{sinh}⁡($\n{{field-2}}\n$)-\\,$\n{{field-3}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537909 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4b85bc81-6104-5328-b444-83c8973655d4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537909 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the following double-angle formula for cosine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the following double-angle formula for the hyperbolic cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2\\theta =1+2{sinh}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n{sinh}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2\\theta -1).\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{2}$, we have\n\n$$\n{sinh}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x-1).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(8{sinh}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})-4)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(4(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x-1)-4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(4\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x-8)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(4\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x-8x)\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(1)-8\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537923 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186537860 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537923 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186537867 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537923 #edb/ref 1069 "q-351903" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537923 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537923 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the following integral.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}(4-3{cosh}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,-\\,$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\operatorname{sinh}⁡($\n{{field-2}}\n$)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537923 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6b367b19-8f35-5f68-a044-eb7b9764c38d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537923 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the following double-angle formula for cosine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -1\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the following double-angle formula for the hyperbolic cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2\\theta =2{cosh}^{2}⁡\\theta -1\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cosh}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2\\theta +1).\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =x$, we have\n\n$$\n{cosh}^{2}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}(4-3{cosh}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}(4-\\frac{3}{2}(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x+1))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}(\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{5}{2}x-\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡2x)|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =[\\frac{5}{2}\\sqrt{2}-\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2\\sqrt{2})]-[0-\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡0] \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{2}-\\frac{3}{4}\\,\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2\\sqrt{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537934 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186537822 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537934 #edb/ref 1069 "q-165874" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537934 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537934 #edb/ref 1071 "${\\int }_{0}^{1/3}(2{sinh}^{2}⁡3x+2{cosh}^{2}⁡3x-1)\\,\\text{d}x=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537934 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7b5373c3-faa7-5442-9a9c-2d5aebc96c49" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537934 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the following double-angle formula for cosine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the following double-angle formula for the hyperbolic cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2\\theta ={cosh}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sinh}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =3x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cosh}⁡6x={cosh}^{2}⁡3x+{sinh}^{2}⁡3x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2{sinh}^{2}⁡3x+2{cosh}^{2}⁡3x-1)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/3}(2({cosh}^{2}⁡3x+{sinh}^{2}⁡3x)-1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/3}(2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡6x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡6x-x){|}_{0}^{1/3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡2-\\frac{1}{3}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\operatorname{sinh}⁡2-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537963 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186537835 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537963 #edb/ref 1069 "q-352419" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537963 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537963 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round your answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(6+6{sinh}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537963 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bc295d1d-76d5-5f67-a844-a3b5be954577" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537963 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the following double-angle formula for cosine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the following double-angle formula for the hyperbolic cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x=1+2{sinh}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n2{sinh}^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x-1.\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(6+6{sinh}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(2+2{sinh}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(2+\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡2x+x)\\,{|}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\  & =3(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =3(\\frac{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-{e}^{-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}}{4}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =3(\\frac{{2}^{2}-{2}^{-2}}{4}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+\\frac{45}{16}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537970 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186537776 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537970 #edb/ref 1069 "q-165889" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537970 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537970 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate \n${\\int }_{0}^{1/2}(3-2{cosh}^{2}⁡3x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537970 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cf4092b0-8e64-55b4-94ba-2a8ea4d2ac81" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537970 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the following double-angle formula for cosine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -1.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the following double-angle formula for the hyperbolic cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2\\theta =2{cosh}^{2}⁡\\theta -1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cosh}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2\\theta +1).\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =3x$, we have\n\n$$\n{cosh}^{2}⁡3x=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡6x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}(3-2{cosh}^{2}⁡3x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}(3-2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡6x+1))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}(3-\\operatorname{cosh}⁡6x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}(2-\\operatorname{cosh}⁡6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(2x-\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡6x)|}_{0}^{1/2} \\\\  & =[2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6\\cdot \\frac{1}{2})]-[2\\cdot 0-\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6\\cdot 0)] \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537971 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186537846 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537971 #edb/ref 1069 "q-352425" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537971 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537971 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round your answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(2-12{sinh}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537971 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d0857a55-78b2-5e38-b682-a21c51974c3c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537971 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the following double-angle formula for cosine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the following double-angle formula for the hyperbolic cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x=1+2{sinh}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n{sinh}^{2}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x-1).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(2-12{sinh}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[2-12\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x-1)]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(8-6\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(8x-3\\operator